            <div xml:id="d69">

                <pb facs="0159" n="69" sameAs="frus:frus1920v02/pg69"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.73/27: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Cuba</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Long</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-12-24T20:00:00-05:29"><hi rendition="#italic">December 24,
                                1920—8 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received December 25—5:35
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>360. This Legation is informed that suspension of the Western Union Telegraph
                    Company’s permit to land at Cojimar was ordered by President Menocal to-day.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Long</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
